WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.000
DOUG KELLY: Welcome
to our session,

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.150
uplevel your data expertise,
professional data engineer

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:20.430
and professional ML
engineer certification.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.310
I'm Doug Kelly and I
now oversee learning

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:24.650
offerings for machine
learning and AI solutions

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.090
on Google Cloud.

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:28.850
Previously, I worked as an ML
engineer and data scientist

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:33.170
at Google Cloud and oversaw data
science content at Coursera.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:35.000
I now spend my time
thinking deeply

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.430
about industrializing
machine learning development

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:40.700
on Google Cloud and driving
the creation of training

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.850
to prepare learners such as
yourselves for data and machine

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:47.150
learning engineering careers.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.340
In this session, I
would like to start off

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:52.970
by discussing two key data and
machine learning challenges

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.500
that enterprises
are facing today.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:59.360
The gap between data platform
investments and realizing value

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:03.320
from them and the scarcity
and corresponding high demand

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.450
for data and machine
learning engineering talent.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:08.880
This will frame our discussion
on how Google Cloud is

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.400
addressing these, both through
data and machine learning

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.700
platform innovations as well
as through our industry leading

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.820
professional certifications,
the professional data

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:22.290
engineer and professional
ML engineer certifications.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.180
I hold both of
these certifications

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.700
and will share my
perspective with you

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.800
on the benefits of
these certifications

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.660
as well as the
recommended learning

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:33.870
path and resources for each.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:35.930
Lastly, I will
give you a preview

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:37.680
of what's coming next
for data and machine

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.890
learning training from
Google Cloud learning.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.780
My goal for the
session is that you

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.660
walk away excited about building
data and machine learning

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.960
solutions on Google Cloud
and you start or level

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.690
up your learning journey
towards certification today.

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:57.460
One of the bigger
challenges for data teams

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:59.800
is turning into a
competitive advantage

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:03.670
the immense, fast growing,
and fast moving amount of data

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:07.190
that our organizations, our
customers, our partners,

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:08.439
our ecosystem is creating.

00:02:10.979 --> 00:02:14.430
According to IDC, 175
zettabytes of data

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:16.900
will be created in
the next five years.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:20.160
One zetabyte equaling
1 trillion gigabytes--

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:23.100
that's 21 zeros.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.170
Our data production
has more than 10xed

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.340
in the last eight years.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.710
In fact, 90% of the
data in the world

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:30.675
has been created in
just the past 10 years.

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:35.350
Yet, when it comes
to turning data

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:39.250
into business outcomes and
business value for companies,

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:41.440
the situation is quite alarming.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.740
Over 2/3 of the data produced
is never actually analyzed.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:47.290
And almost 70% of
companies say they're

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:53.670
unable to realize tangible and
measurable value from data.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:57.090
The key takeaway is this,
delivering value with analytics

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:59.640
and machine learning
requires a modern data

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:02.560
platform such as Google Cloud.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:06.100
Data engineers are essential
to build, operate, and maintain

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:09.280
these data platforms to
enable business value.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:12.220
And machine learning
engineers, in turn,

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:14.650
build and deploy machine
learning solutions

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:18.910
on top of a robust data platform
to drive decision making

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:20.350
and the realization of value.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.720
Data engineers and ML
engineers work closely together

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.820
on data teams to
close the data value

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:31.850
gap by tightly integrating
data and machine

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:34.030
learning infrastructure.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:36.010
In industry, we know
that machine learning

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:40.000
has had the most business impact
by scaling real-time decision

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.460
making and personalization.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:44.320
That means we have to act fast.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:47.950
To do so, we need data engineers
enabling data processing

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.440
and analytics speed
and ML engineers

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:53.750
to deliver predictions that
arrive at the point of action

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.400
and real time.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.910
That's the difference between
discovering and preventing

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.910
fraud, purchases and
cart abandonment,

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:03.745
and proactive and
reactive customer service.

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:10.370
Google Cloud is simplifying data
analytics and machine learning

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:12.290
through each of
the platform design

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:14.510
pillars outlined on this slide.

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:17.660
We deliver serverless
analytics, allowing customers

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:21.350
to keep development velocity
high and their focus purely

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:24.140
on analytics versus
infrastructure.

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:28.310
We offer a comprehensive set
of data analytics workloads,

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:32.270
from batch and streaming data
processing to data warehousing

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:34.220
to business intelligence.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:36.320
We provide the services
for our customers

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:39.260
to operationalize machine
learning solutions,

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:45.860
from pre-built ML APIs to
AutoML to BigQuery ML to custom

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:48.350
TensorFlow and PyTorch models.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:52.190
We enable the best open source
data technologies to give you

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:54.630
flexibility and choice.

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:57.830
And we build for enterprise data
and machine learning workloads

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:58.595
at any scale.

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:05.370
Google Cloud is already a
recognized industry leader

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:08.790
with a purpose built, end-to-end
data analytics and machine

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:12.540
learning platform to support
the entire data team anywhere,

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:15.340
on premise or on Google Cloud.

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:18.400
Data engineers are able to
leverage services like Pub/Sub,

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:22.300
Dataflow, and Data Fusion to
ingest, prepare, and transform

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.720
data at any scale.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.820
They can also leverage
new data services

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.640
like data plaques and
analytics hub and market

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.640
leading analytics services,
such as BigQuery and Looker,

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.400
to manage and quickly
surface enterprise data

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:39.590
sets and insights to
the entire organization.

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:41.450
Announced at Google
I/O this year,

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:44.330
Vertex AI is also rolling
out as the successor

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:47.630
to AI platform for machine
learning development.

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:51.470
It provides ML engineers with
an integrated suite of services

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:55.090
to help enable each stage
of your ML workflow,

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:59.330
from gathering data to feature
engineering to building models

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.480
and, finally, deploying
and moderneering

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:03.930
these models in production.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.660
For example, new
Vertex MLop services,

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:09.330
like Pipelines
and Feature Store,

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:14.160
give ML engineers
reusable ML workflows

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:17.430
while Vertex Predictions
gives ML engineers

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:20.190
a scalable, serverless
solution to get

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:23.115
model predictions into
decision making UIs faster.

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:29.660
Depending upon how you define
the machine learning market,

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:33.520
if you look at platforms like
Qwiklabs, Kaggle, Coursera,

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:36.970
and LinkedIn, there
are only about 300,000

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:39.925
global professional data
engineers, data scientists,

00:06:39.925 --> 00:06:42.680
and ML engineers today.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:45.620
Yet, at the same time, there's
huge demand for data engineers

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:48.250
and ML engineers in the market.

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:50.290
According to Coursera
market research,

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:52.510
in just the past
12 months, there's

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:56.560
been over 200,000 job postings
requiring data engineering

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.770
and ML engineering
skills, and that demand

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:01.360
has been trending upwards.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:02.950
Over the past three
years, there's

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:07.360
been a 91% increase in job
postings requiring these skill

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.680
sets.

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:10.960
Many enterprises are
still in the early stages

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:14.350
of data platform
modernization and AI adoption

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:18.060
and are really struggling to
find data engineers and ML

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:21.010
engineers to make this happen.

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:24.280
To bridge the skills gap, Google
Cloud learning has brought some

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:28.060
of the best of Google
together, its top engineers,

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:32.110
it's solutions and expertise
in building large scale data

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:36.670
and machine learning systems
to produce two industry leading

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:39.760
certifications in the job
market, the professional data

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:43.210
engineer and
professional ML engineer.

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:45.700
These certifications are
not just about Google Cloud

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:46.970
technologies.

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:51.460
In fact, the initial stages of
designing each certification

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:53.350
are product agnostic.

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:55.120
And just like the
real world examinees

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.220
are expected to
know the vast amount

00:07:57.220 --> 00:08:01.060
of foundational concepts, design
patterns, and technology trade

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:04.990
offs that they may encounter
in their day to day jobs.

00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:08.400
So how have these certifications
been received by learners

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:10.080
and recognized in
the job market?

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:14.960
Think of Google
Cloud certifications

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:17.840
as valuable tools to
validate your learning

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:22.430
and help you build your career,
get promoted, and earn raises.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:25.400
In a recent survey of Google
Cloud certified individuals

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.840
conducted by an
independent third party,

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:29.960
we heard some incredible
pieces of feedback

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:34.700
from learners across the job
market on how Google Cloud

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:39.530
certifications have enabled and
boosted skills for Cloud roles.

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:42.679
78% of respondents
were more confident

00:08:42.679 --> 00:08:45.020
when talking about their
future opportunities

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:46.970
after certification.

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:50.150
82% of respondents felt
proud to have a proof

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:52.130
point about their
skills and abilities

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:54.470
when working with recruiters.

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:58.370
83% of respondents told us
they felt more marketable.

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:01.970
And finally, 85%
of respondents just

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:04.580
had the boost of confidence
that they both wanted

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:07.100
and needed to really
get themselves out there

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.470
for Cloud opportunities.

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:12.920
So in short, if you're asking
yourself, what's in it for me,

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:16.000
I hope these anecdotal
shares and statistics drive

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:17.920
home how learners
like yourselves

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:22.180
have benefited from Google
Cloud certifications.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:24.190
Next, let's take a
look a little bit more

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:26.530
closely at the
value propositions

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:29.320
for the professional data
engineer and ML engineer

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:30.370
certifications.

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:35.530
First, let's talk about the
professional data engineer

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:36.740
certification.

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:39.490
A professional data
engineer is the enabler

00:09:39.490 --> 00:09:43.480
of data driven decision making
by collecting, transforming,

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:45.470
and publishing data.

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:48.160
This is an intermediate
professional certification

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:51.010
that requires three-plus
years of industry experience

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:53.380
and one-plus years
designing and managing

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:56.180
data solutions on Google Cloud.

00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:58.130
We offer a data
engineering learning

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:00.980
path with hands-on
practice through Qwiklabs

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:03.620
that culminates in a
two hour multiple choice

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:06.710
and multi select exam
to validate your ability

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:10.220
to design, build, and
operationalize data processing

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:11.720
systems.

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:15.380
Upon completion, you earn a
shareable credential and gain

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:20.405
access to Google Cloud
community, swag, and events.

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:25.710
So why do I think you should
get certified as a Google Cloud

00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:27.460
data engineer?

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:30.520
Data engineering is a
challenging applied discipline

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:33.140
that is best learned
through practice.

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:35.230
Through following the
recommended learning path,

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:38.770
you will complete 30 plus
hands on data engineering labs

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:41.620
in a sandbox GCP
project environment

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:43.210
to practice building
and deploying

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:45.610
data processing solutions.

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:48.310
Further, the Google Cloud
data engineer certification

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:50.920
was recently named
as the number one

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:55.420
top paid global IT certification
according to global knowledge

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:57.480
market research.

00:10:57.480 --> 00:10:59.730
You will learn some of the
most valuable and in-demand

00:10:59.730 --> 00:11:02.010
enterprise skills
in the market and be

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:05.340
indispensable to organizations
modernizing their data

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:10.050
platforms and looking to
adopt machine learning.

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:12.570
Third, you will learn data
engineering best practices

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:16.620
from Google, which brought
Hadoop and Beam to the world

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:20.970
and currently processes over
2.5 exabytes of logs per

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:25.150
month on planet scale
compute in network.

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:28.330
Through this certification,
you will differentiate yourself

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:31.510
for career success by learning
how to choose the right data

00:11:31.510 --> 00:11:35.260
storage and processing services,
identify the right balance

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:37.720
of trade offs for
various data workloads,

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:40.960
and practice implementing
production tested data

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:42.355
processing design patterns.

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:49.510
To prepare you for the exam,
we designed a learning path

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:52.090
that covers foundational
data concepts

00:11:52.090 --> 00:11:54.790
and data pipeline design
patterns as well as

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:59.770
steps you progressively through
key data ingestion, storage,

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:04.000
and data transformation
services on Google Cloud.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.700
For aspiring data
engineers, the learning path

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:09.640
is designed to be completed
in about three and 1/2 months

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:12.360
and about five hours per week.

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:15.540
For existing data engineers,
the Coursera preparation

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:17.070
certificate is
still a great place

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:21.120
to start to learn Google Cloud
data services that you can then

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:23.970
supplement as needed with
additional hands-on practice

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:25.810
through Qwiklabs.

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:28.750
I recommend the certification
to ML engineers, as well,

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:30.940
and personally started
my certification journey

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:32.570
here first.

00:12:32.570 --> 00:12:34.730
Data management
and data processing

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:39.260
are key foundations of modern
production ML pipelines.

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:44.430
Now, let's discuss the
professional ML engineer

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.270
certification.

00:12:46.270 --> 00:12:48.540
This is a more
advanced certification

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:52.050
that also recommends three-plus
years of industry experience

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:54.960
as a data scientist or
machine learning engineer,

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:58.500
including at least one
year designing and managing

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:01.870
machine learning
solutions on Google Cloud.

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:04.990
A professional ML
engineer designs, builds,

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:08.830
and production houses ML models
to solve business challenges

00:13:08.830 --> 00:13:14.950
using Google Cloud ML services
and knowledge of proven ML

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:18.990
models and techniques.

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:21.740
So why do I think you should get
certified as a Google Cloud ML

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:23.350
engineer?

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:26.410
The Google Cloud professional
ML engineer certification

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:30.250
is continuously updated by
leading Googler and industry

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:33.760
subject matter experts to
best reflect the ML engineer

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:36.530
skill set in the job market.

00:13:36.530 --> 00:13:39.380
This gives aspiring and
current ML engineers

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:42.470
the opportunity to validate
their expertise in machine

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:46.670
learning in Google Cloud against
a rigorous, practical industry

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:51.760
benchmark exam recognized
in the job market.

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:54.100
Google is a globally
recognized leader

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:56.770
in AI research and
applied machine learning

00:13:56.770 --> 00:14:00.010
with over a decade of
experience productionizing

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:03.160
machine learning systems as
part of applications serving

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:06.310
billions of users per day.

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:08.980
Google Cloud is the
platform by which

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:12.220
Google delivers this pioneering
ML research and product

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:14.510
solutions to customers.

00:14:14.510 --> 00:14:16.690
In fact, Google
Cloud's AI platform

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:21.280
was recognized by Gartner as
an industry leader in its 2020

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:25.630
Magic Quadrant for Cloud
AI developer services.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:28.780
My key takeaways on the ML
engineer certification for you

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:30.680
all are this.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:34.310
The Google Cloud professional
ML engineering certification

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:36.800
is a rewarding learning
journey for you

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:40.400
to build your development skills
on an industry-leading data

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:44.300
and machine learning platform to
both differentiate yourself as

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:47.370
well as position yourself
for success in the rapidly

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:49.730
evolving field of
applied machine learning.

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:55.650
The learning path is designed
to augment your study

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:59.430
through a structured progression
of role based curriculum

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:01.380
through Google
Cloud fundamentals

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:06.030
through applied machine learning
and up to ML ops content.

00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:09.000
It's designed to be completed
in about four months

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:11.460
at about six hours per week.

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:13.170
The content is
available on demand

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:16.830
through a Coursera professional
certification certificate

00:15:16.830 --> 00:15:19.590
with additional hands-on
practice opportunities

00:15:19.590 --> 00:15:22.140
available through Qwiklabs.

00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:25.590
For aspiring ML engineers,
I have two additional tips

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:27.160
for you.

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:31.050
First, take advantage of $300
in free credits in the Google

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:35.310
Cloud free tier on products
such as the ML APIs AutoML

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:39.800
and BigQuery to start building
ML applications today.

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:42.440
Second, learn
socially and publicly.

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:45.080
Form a study group to share
your learnings and projects

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:46.820
with others.

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:49.760
GitHub, blogs, or the
Google Cloud learning forums

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:52.210
are a great place to start.

00:15:52.210 --> 00:15:54.150
I personally like open
source contributions

00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:56.845
to projects, tutorials,
and documentation.

00:15:56.845 --> 00:15:59.220
Take a look at open issues on
some of your favorite email

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:02.760
projects like TensorFlow
and Google Cloud samples

00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:05.460
tagged as help-wanted
or good first issue

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:07.350
as an approachable
place to dive in.

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:12.950
Lastly, I'd like to share
with you all of what's

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:15.440
coming next for Google Cloud
data and machine learning

00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:17.120
training.

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:19.700
It's an exciting time to be
building data and machine

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:20.960
learning solutions.

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:25.070
So far in 2021, Google Cloud's
already industry leading data

00:16:25.070 --> 00:16:26.660
and machine learning
platform has

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:29.270
seen its most significant
enhancements in the past two

00:16:29.270 --> 00:16:31.320
to three years.

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:35.790
In the June 2021 data summit,
Google Cloud engineering teams

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:38.070
laid out their vision
for the data cloud

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:41.550
with new services like
Dataplex and Analytics Hub

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:45.180
to bring new data management and
analytics sharing capabilities

00:16:45.180 --> 00:16:47.580
to enterprise data teams.

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:51.600
Together, along with new
integrations between BigQuery

00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:55.620
and Booker, data engineers can
focus on further breaking down

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:59.850
organizational data silos
to more broadly socialize

00:16:59.850 --> 00:17:05.300
insights across organizations
to enable business value.

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:09.530
Furthermore, at
Google IO in May 2021,

00:17:09.530 --> 00:17:11.810
Google Cloud
announced Vertex AIs,

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:16.099
the successor to AI Platform,
a unification of services

00:17:16.099 --> 00:17:18.560
such as AutoML and
custom training

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:21.960
for developing ML
solutions faster.

00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:25.290
There are over 20-plus major
updates and net new services

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:29.700
reaching GA over the next
year, particularly related

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:33.330
to ML ops, opening up
fundamentally new ways

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:36.660
to build and deploy ML
solutions and incorporate them

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:41.620
into decision making systems
to deliver business value.

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:44.920
Vertex AI, BigQuery,
and Looker, as well as

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:49.360
AI industry solutions empower
data scientists or data

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:52.480
engineers and ML
engineers with new tools

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:55.840
to close the data value gap
while enhancing development

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:59.110
and productivity, the ability
to scale your workflow

00:17:59.110 --> 00:18:02.080
and your decision
making with your data,

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:06.200
as well as accelerating
time to value.

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:09.230
My colleagues and I in
Cloud Learning services

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:14.210
are hard at work bringing Data
Cloud, Vertex AI, and industry

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:18.510
solutions content to you
through Qwiklabs and Coursera.

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:20.520
Stay tuned for
significant new data

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:22.740
and machine learning
training rolling out

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:25.710
in the second half of
this year as well as

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:28.290
a major update to the
professional ML engineer

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:34.020
certification for Vertex AI
in the second half of 2022.

00:18:34.020 --> 00:18:36.750
Now, I'm keen to switch over
to the Google Cloud console

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:42.370
to share with you some of the
new capabilities of Vertex AI.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:45.490
Welcome to the Vertex AI
ML development platform

00:18:45.490 --> 00:18:47.590
in the Google Cloud console.

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:49.930
To get started, first
enable the Vertex service

00:18:49.930 --> 00:18:52.210
in the API and Services tab.

00:18:54.790 --> 00:18:57.550
Vertex AI is a platform
that contains services

00:18:57.550 --> 00:19:00.370
for each phase of the ML
development lifecycle,

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:03.760
from data sets to
predictions, enabling

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:06.490
you to go from experimentation
to production ML

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:10.990
workflows to delivering
business value faster.

00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:13.990
The Data Sets tab contains
a list of all your data

00:19:13.990 --> 00:19:19.240
sets in your project with
support for image, tabular,

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:22.370
text, and video data types.

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:25.300
Manage data sets enable you to
create a link between your data

00:19:25.300 --> 00:19:28.930
sets and your models for
traceable and reproducible

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:32.080
experiments.

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:36.250
You also get descriptive
statistics on your data set

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:40.450
as well as the ability to
configure automatic or custom

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:43.340
data splitting.

00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:47.150
The Notebooks tab contains new
features such as Managed Vertex

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:47.900
Notebooks.

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:55.180
Vertex Notebooks are interactive
JupyterLab development

00:19:55.180 --> 00:19:58.210
environments that enable
you to quickly build custom

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:00.130
machine learning solutions.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:02.830
They provide support
for multiple frameworks

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:06.940
flexible compute and easy
access to accelerators

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:11.120
like GPUs and TPUs.

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:13.310
They also have newer,
tighter integrations

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.650
with key Google
Cloud data services,

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:28.830
like Cloud Storage and
BigQuery in a single window.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:31.680
Check out some of the newer
integrations with Data PROC

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:34.560
as well, which also
makes Vertex notebooks

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:38.820
a great single window for
development of Apache spark,

00:20:38.820 --> 00:20:39.480
as well.

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:52.070
In the Training tab you can also
see and create your training

00:20:52.070 --> 00:20:57.440
pipelines using the same
managed data set for both AutoML

00:20:57.440 --> 00:20:58.715
and custom training jobs.

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:07.610
You can leverage pre-built
containers with your model code

00:21:07.610 --> 00:21:11.600
with frameworks like TensorFlow,
Scikit-learn, PyTorch,

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:13.760
or XGBoost.

00:21:13.760 --> 00:21:15.770
For maxima; flexibility,
you can also

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:20.030
leverage custom containers, as
well, leverage in any framework

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:23.570
you'd like with any
additional dependencies,

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:26.480
upload it to artifact
registry, and use it

00:21:26.480 --> 00:21:29.600
for model, training, prediction,
or as a pipeline step.

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:37.510
AutoML is a great way to quickly
build highly accurate models

00:21:37.510 --> 00:21:41.620
with built-in support for
standard evaluation metrics,

00:21:41.620 --> 00:21:45.910
feature attributions,
quick model deployment,

00:21:45.910 --> 00:21:49.630
as well as metadata that
covers the model architecture

00:21:49.630 --> 00:21:51.850
search as well as the
hyperparameters that

00:21:51.850 --> 00:21:55.150
were searched, as well.

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:58.900
In the Experiments tab, you can
create a managed TensorBoard

00:21:58.900 --> 00:22:03.730
instance to organize and compare
model performance across model

00:22:03.730 --> 00:22:05.170
runs and data splits.

00:22:15.030 --> 00:22:17.850
For predictions, you
can deploy new endpoints

00:22:17.850 --> 00:22:22.070
for online predictions
or scheduled batch jobs

00:22:22.070 --> 00:22:25.460
for bulk predictions, as well.

00:22:25.460 --> 00:22:27.980
A model can be deployed
to multiple endpoints

00:22:27.980 --> 00:22:32.480
or can serve multiple
models on a single endpoint.

00:22:32.480 --> 00:22:35.570
With multiple models on a single
endpoint and traffic splitting

00:22:35.570 --> 00:22:39.170
capabilities, you now have some
new model prediction evaluation

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:43.300
capabilities, such
as A/B testing.

00:22:43.300 --> 00:22:47.260
For production ML workflows,
the new Vertex pipeline service

00:22:47.260 --> 00:22:50.770
enables you to automate,
monitor, and govern

00:22:50.770 --> 00:22:53.980
your machine learning systems
by orchestrating your tasks

00:22:53.980 --> 00:22:55.780
in a serverless manner.

00:22:55.780 --> 00:22:58.120
Clicking into an
individual pipeline run,

00:22:58.120 --> 00:23:00.430
you have a graphical
user interface

00:23:00.430 --> 00:23:03.220
to view and debug each
step of your workflow,

00:23:03.220 --> 00:23:07.600
from data set creation,
model training, evaluation,

00:23:07.600 --> 00:23:09.610
and deployment.

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:11.560
You can expand
upon your artifacts

00:23:11.560 --> 00:23:15.130
to be able to deep dive
into individual pipeline

00:23:15.130 --> 00:23:19.765
runs and their artifacts, such
as model evaluation metrics.

00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:26.660
In this example, you also have
a conditional model deployment

00:23:26.660 --> 00:23:29.240
step, which you
can use to ensure

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:31.190
that you're only pushing
higher performing

00:23:31.190 --> 00:23:34.320
models to production.

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:36.180
This concludes a
quick walkthrough

00:23:36.180 --> 00:23:39.490
of just some of the new
features available in Vertex AI.

00:23:39.490 --> 00:23:41.280
I encourage you
to also check out

00:23:41.280 --> 00:23:47.790
services like data labeling,
ML metadata for tracking

00:23:47.790 --> 00:23:50.220
your development artifacts
across your project,

00:23:50.220 --> 00:23:52.830
as well as the upcoming
Feature Store, which

00:23:52.830 --> 00:23:57.840
enables you to reuse
features across ML use cases.

00:23:57.840 --> 00:24:00.540
For hands-on on practice in a
Google Cloud project with some

00:24:00.540 --> 00:24:02.940
of the features I just
introduced, check out

00:24:02.940 --> 00:24:05.970
the Vertex AI labs on Qwiklabs.

00:24:05.970 --> 00:24:10.630
A great place to start is
the Vertex AI Qwik Start,

00:24:10.630 --> 00:24:13.330
where you will walk through
an end-to-end custom training

00:24:13.330 --> 00:24:17.740
workflow on Vertex AI
to train and deploy

00:24:17.740 --> 00:24:23.600
a TensorFlow model to predict
customer lifetime value.

00:24:23.600 --> 00:24:26.300
To start your data and
machine learning engineering

00:24:26.300 --> 00:24:29.240
learning journeys today, check
out our recently launched

00:24:29.240 --> 00:24:32.330
Google Cloud Skills
Boost, our new destination

00:24:32.330 --> 00:24:36.660
for Google Cloud learning with
over 700 labs and courses.

00:24:36.660 --> 00:24:40.070
This will be available to you
all the entire month of October

00:24:40.070 --> 00:24:41.980
free of charge.

00:24:41.980 --> 00:24:44.650
It's never been a more
exciting and productive time

00:24:44.650 --> 00:24:48.380
to be building data systems and
doing applied machine learning.

00:24:48.380 --> 00:24:50.820
Thank you for learning with us.

